tools.description:
Close browser tabs by one selection mode: `tab_ids` (explicit), `match` (substring of title/URL), or `duplicates` (every tab sharing a URL with an earlier one). Set `dry_run` to preview the exact tabs that would close without touching them. `match` and `duplicates` leave pinned tabs open unless `include_pinned` is true. Closing more than 10 tabs needs `expected_count`, the count from the preview that the user agreed to; if the selection no longer has exactly that many tabs, nothing closes. This tool cannot reopen what it closes (reopen_tabs can, from a record saved by snapshot_tabs).

Ask the user before running with dry_run=false, naming what will close and how many, unless they already asked for exactly this close.

Examples:
- {"match": "github.com", "dry_run": true}
- {"match": "github.com", "expected_count": 14}
- {"tab_ids": ["firefox:12", "firefox:13"]}
- {"duplicates": true, "dry_run": true}

Returns:
  JSON object containing:
  - dry_run (boolean): Whether this was a preview
  - reason (string): Description of selection criteria
  - count/closed (int): Number of tabs matched/closed
  - pinned_kept (int): Pinned tabs that matched but were left open
  - by_domain (object): Map of domain to count
  - sample (array): First 10 tabs with {id, title, url}
